-/// drives end-to-end. See <c>docs/demo/README.md</c>.
+/// GET /tasks supports an optional <c>?status=</c> filter (case-insensitive, over the
+/// <see cref="TaskState"/> names). A <c>?priority=</c> filter is still open. Filtering lives here,
+/// at the endpoint/query boundary — the store's public shape is unchanged (architecture posture,
